## 6. How to Use Modules in HTML

To use JavaScript modules in a browser, add `type="module"` to your script tag.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>JavaScript Modules</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Learning JavaScript Modules</h1>

    <script type="module" src="./main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

Your folder structure could look like this:

```text
my-project/
├── index.html
├── main.js
├── math.js
└── greet.js
```

Run the project using a local development server. Browsers commonly restrict module imports when an HTML file is opened directly through `file://`.

